{#
   Live Telemetry (#telemetry) — the Boardroom Incident & Consequence Feed.

   Was _chairmans_terminal.html.twig, a widget in the right-hand column of the
   hero. The redesign promotes it to a full-bleed section of its own: the feed
   now needs a pause control, a four-tile stat strip and a per-line button
   target, none of which fits beside hero copy.

   Real, live data only (refreshed by app:telemetry:generate) — no illustrative
   filler. That constraint predates this redesign and still governs every line
   here. See LiveTelemetryService for exactly how each figure and each feed
   category is built; the short version:
     - fixturesSimulated / getCapitalDeployedFormatted() / getResultsFormatted() /
       activeClubs / weeksPlayed — aggregated from recent SyncRecord payloads.
       weeksPlayed is sync count * 4 (each sync ~= 4 on-device weekly ticks), an
       approximation rather than a true weeks-elapsed count.
     - totalGoals / getGoalsPerMatchFormatted() and tableTurnover — pyramid-wide
       collective totals. Goals are summed from fixtures[] deduplicated by
       fixtureId, since each payload carries the syncing club's whole division's
       round and several clubs report the same fixtures. Table Turnover counts
       SeasonRecord promotions/relegations over the feed's 7-day window, not the
       stats window: a season concludes far more rarely than a sync, so a 24h
       count would read 0 almost permanently.
     - recentEvents — up to 20 items across 9 real sources, selected round-robin
       (selectBalanced()) so a rare category can't be crowded out, then re-sorted
       newest-first. Each carries {time, text, category, categoryLabel, club,
       clubId, clubs, detail, amountExact, timestampIso, meta, dossier}.

   THREE STATES, per design/States.dc.html. The distinction that matters is
   "never generated" vs "generated and everything was zero" — a zero snapshot is
   a real, reportable state and must not read as a broken cron:
     - not generated: no row at all (getId() === null), so every figure is a
       default rather than a measurement. Tiles render as em-dashes, not zeros.
     - stale: generated, but longer ago than the cron's own cadence allows.
     - active: everything else.

   STALE_AFTER_SECONDS is 1800 here and in Api\TelemetryController, which is a
   duplicated constant: the API endpoint computes `stale` server-side, but this
   page is rendered from the entity directly (LandingController passes
   LiveTelemetryService::getSnapshot(), never a round trip to its own API) and
   the entity carries no staleness accessor. Keep the two numbers in step, or
   the page and the endpoint will disagree about the same snapshot.
#}
{% set telemetry_generated = telemetry.id is not null %}
{% set telemetry_age = 'now'|date('U') - telemetry.generatedAt|date('U') %}
{% set telemetry_stale = telemetry_generated and telemetry_age > 1800 %}
{% set telemetry_state = not telemetry_generated ? 'pending' : (telemetry_stale ? 'stale' : 'active') %}

<section class="telemetry-section" id="telemetry" aria-labelledby="telemetry-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="terminal is-{{ telemetry_state }}">
            <div class="terminal-header">
                <div class="terminal-header-live">
                    <span class="terminal-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <h2 class="pixel terminal-title" id="telemetry-title">
                        {%- if telemetry_state == 'pending' -%}
                            TELEMETRY // AWAITING FIRST REFRESH
                        {%- elseif telemetry_state == 'stale' -%}
                            TELEMETRY // STALE SYNC
                        {%- else -%}
                            LIVE TELEMETRY // 24H PYRAMID FEED
                        {%- endif -%}
                    </h2>
                </div>
                <span class="terminal-sync vt">
                    {%- if telemetry_state == 'pending' -%}
                        SYNC: AWAITING FIRST REFRESH
                    {%- elseif telemetry_state == 'stale' -%}
                        SYNC: DELAYED [LAST REFRESH {{ telemetry.generatedAt|date('H:i') }}, {{ (telemetry_age / 60)|round(0, 'floor') }} MIN AGO]
                    {%- else -%}
                        SYNC: ACTIVE [REFRESHED {{ telemetry.generatedAt|date('H:i') }}]
                    {%- endif -%}
                </span>
            </div>

            {#
               Four tiles. Each big pixel-font value stays a bare number with the
               descriptive text in the smaller sub-line — a full sentence in the
               pixel font wraps and overflows the tile.

               An ungenerated snapshot shows an em-dash rather than 0: a real
               pyramid-wide zero and "we have never measured this" look identical
               as numerals, and only one of them is a figure.
            #}
            <div class="terminal-stats">
                <div class="terminal-stat">
                    <span class="terminal-stat-label pixel">Fixtures &amp; Form</span>
                    <span class="terminal-stat-val">{{ telemetry_generated ? telemetry.fixturesSimulated|number_format : '—' }}</span>
                    <span class="terminal-stat-sub vt">{{ telemetry_generated ? telemetry.getResultsFormatted() ~ ' (W-D-L)' : 'No snapshot yet' }}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="terminal-stat">
                    <span class="terminal-stat-label pixel">Capital Deployed</span>
                    <span class="terminal-stat-val is-mint">{{ telemetry_generated ? telemetry.getCapitalDeployedFormatted() : '—' }}</span>
                    <span class="terminal-stat-sub vt">Transfers &amp; infra</span>
                </div>
                <div class="terminal-stat">
                    <span class="terminal-stat-label pixel">Goals Logged</span>
                    <span class="terminal-stat-val is-gold">{{ telemetry_generated ? telemetry.totalGoals|number_format : '—' }}</span>
                    <span class="terminal-stat-sub vt">{{ telemetry_generated ? telemetry.getGoalsPerMatchFormatted() : 'No snapshot yet' }}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="terminal-stat">
                    <span class="terminal-stat-label pixel">Table Turnover</span>
                    <span class="terminal-stat-val is-red">{{ telemetry_generated ? telemetry.tableTurnover|number_format : '—' }}</span>
                    <span class="terminal-stat-sub vt">Promotions &amp; drops, 7 days</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="terminal-body">
                {#
                   One real <button> per line, inside a list item. These used to be
                   divs carrying tabindex="0" role="button" plus a keydown shim for
                   Enter/Space in landing.js — a button gets all of that from the
                   platform, including the right focus ring and the right behaviour
                   for assistive tech that enumerates controls.
                #}
                <ul class="terminal-feed" aria-label="Recent pyramid activity">
                    {% for event in telemetry.recentEvents %}
                        <li class="terminal-feed-row">
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="terminal-feed-item{{ loop.first ? ' active' }} vt cat-{{ event.category|lower }}"
                                    data-category-label="{{ event.categoryLabel }}"
                                    data-club="{{ event.club }}"
                                    data-detail="{{ event.detail }}"
                                    data-amount="{{ event.amountExact }}"
                                    data-timestamp="{{ event.timestampIso }}"
                                    data-meta="{{ event.meta|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}"
                                    data-club-badge="{{ event.clubBadge|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}"
                                    data-dossier="{{ event.dossier|default(null)|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}">
                                <span class="terminal-feed-category pixel">{{ event.categoryLabel }}</span>
                                <span class="terminal-feed-line">
                                    {#
                                       A badge per club the line NAMES, not just the first.
                                       event.clubs is [{name, clubId, badge}] in the order the
                                       names appear, with the primary club at index 0; a
                                       transfer names two sides and the design draws both.

                                       A null badge means "no Club row behind this name" (an
                                       NPC side, typically), not "kit unset" — those slots
                                       carry no data-club-badge at all and landing.js leaves
                                       them empty rather than drawing a default kit and
                                       implying a club that does not exist.
                                    #}
                                    {% for named in event.clubs|default([]) %}
                                        {% if named.badge %}
                                            <span class="terminal-feed-badge"
                                                  data-club-badge="{{ named.badge|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}"
                                                  aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                        {% endif %}
                                    {% endfor %}
                                    <span class="terminal-feed-time">[{{ event.time }}]</span> {{ event.text }}
                                </span>
                            </button>
                        </li>
                    {% else %}
                        <li class="terminal-feed-row">
                            <p class="terminal-feed-empty vt">
                                {%- if telemetry_generated -%}
                                    No activity to report in the last 24 hours.
                                {%- else -%}
                                    No activity to report yet. The first snapshot lands within 15 minutes of the next refresh.
                                {%- endif -%}
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ul>

                <div class="terminal-aside">
                    <div>
                        <div class="terminal-aside-title pixel">INCIDENT REPORT</div>
                        <p class="terminal-aside-copy">Select any line to open the boardroom dossier: the club's badge and kit, the logged time, the value, its best-rated player and its latest fixtures.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="terminal-aside-actions">
                        {#
                           Hidden when there is nothing to rotate — a pause control
                           over a single line (or none) is a dead toggle. Its pressed
                           state and label are owned by landing.js, which also starts
                           it already paused under prefers-reduced-motion.
                        #}
                        {% if telemetry.recentEvents|length > 1 %}
                            <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm pixel" id="telemetry-pause" aria-pressed="false">PAUSE FEED</button>
                        {% endif %}
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-gold btn-sm pixel" id="terminal-cta">ENTER BOARDROOM</button>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="terminal-footer vt">
                {% if telemetry_generated %}
                    {{ telemetry.activeClubs|number_format }} ACTIVE CLUBS // ~{{ telemetry.weeksPlayed|number_format }} WEEKS PLAYED (ESTIMATE) // OFFLINE-FIRST ENGINE.
                    Results are tallied from the last five matches per sync, so a club that syncs often can be counted twice.
                {% else %}
                    OFFLINE-FIRST ENGINE. Figures appear once the first snapshot is generated.
                {% endif %}
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
